cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Matched-Magnitude Controls for Causal Testing of
  Spectral Mechanisms in Attention
message: >-
  If you use this note, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Evgeny
    family-names: Vyaltsev
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0004-3712-6798'
  - given-names: Daniil
    family-names: Vyaltsev
abstract: >-
  A short methodological note on causal testing of spectral
  mechanistic claims in attention. It shows why an ablation of a
  dominant spectral mode must control for perturbation magnitude,
  gives a worked example in which a naive construction produced a
  treatment perturbation 10-30x larger than its control, and
  describes a three-part framework -- matched-magnitude
  intervention, random-spectrum baseline, pre-registered outcome
  criteria -- that converts the same hypothesis into a correct
  pre-registered null.
keywords:
  - causal testing
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - spectral analysis
  - attention
  - ablation
  - experimental methodology
